KrakenSDR suite - licences
==========================

Copyright (c) 2026 KrakenRF Inc.

The KrakenSDR suite is made of separate programs under different licences:

  heimdall_v2/       Heimdall receiver server        GNU General Public License
                                                     version 3 or later
                                                     (heimdall_v2/LICENSE)

  gr-krakensdr_v2/   GNU Radio module                GNU General Public License
                                                     version 3 or later
                                                     (gr-krakensdr_v2/LICENSE)

  kraken_doa_v2/     KrakenSDR DoA software,         KrakenSDR Source Available
                     including its decoder plugins   Licence 1.0
                     and their library plugins/lib   (kraken_doa_v2/LICENSE)
                     - except the parts below

  The plugin SDK: kraken_doa_v2/plugins/sdk/,        MIT License
  kraken_doa_v2/plugins/SDK.md, and the Windows      (kraken_doa_v2/plugins/sdk/
  process helpers every program of the suite         LICENSE)
  links (kraken_doa_v2/win/ and heimdall_v2/win/)

  A decoder plugin folder kraken_doa_v2/plugins/<id>/ that holds a LICENSE
  file of its own is under that licence:
    plugins/ism/     ISM device decoder (follows     GNU General Public License
                     rtl_433's decoders)             version 2 or later
                                                     (plugins/ism/LICENSE)
    plugins/flarm/   FLARM / OGN trackers (the OGN   GNU General Public License
                     parity-check matrix from the    version 3
                     OGN project's diy-tracker)      (plugins/flarm/LICENSE)

  The build, install, run and packaging scripts in the repository root
  (install.sh, install-pi-service.sh, run.sh, run.bat, build_windows.bat,
  Dockerfile, docker-compose.yml) and in docker/, windows/, scripts/ and
  .githooks/                                         MIT License (below)

  The documentation in the repository root (README.md, DOCKER.md,
  WINDOWS.md, CLAUDE.md)                             KrakenSDR Source Available
                                                     Licence 1.0

The KrakenSDR DoA software is free for personal and hobbyist use, and
organisations may evaluate it free of charge for up to 90 days (testing, not
yet relying on it in their work). Deploying it and other commercial use need
a licence from KrakenRF Inc. - contact krakenrf@krakensdr.com. Commercial
licences include kraken_doa_v2/COMMERCIAL_TERMS.md.

The programs communicate with each other over network connections (TCP ports
8091 / 8092); each one is used and distributed under its own licence. Files
that appear in more than one program (the portability helpers under
heimdall_v2/src/core and kraken_doa_v2/include/utils, external/pffft ...) are
under the licence of the program whose folder they are in; the Windows
helpers (heimdall_v2/win, kraken_doa_v2/win) are MIT in both.

Every decoder plugin is a program of its own too: kraken_doa starts it as a
separate process and exchanges samples and results with it through pipes, in
the protocol documented in kraken_doa_v2/plugins/sdk/kraken_plugin.hpp. A
plugin under a licence of its own is built only from its own files, the MIT
plugin SDK, pffft and liquid-dsp - never from kraken_doa_v2/plugins/lib or
the rest of kraken_doa (kraken_doa_v2/plugins/Makefile enforces this). Its
licence therefore covers that plugin alone, not kraken_doa or the other
plugins, and theirs doesn't cover it.

Third-party components keep their own licences; see
heimdall_v2/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and kraken_doa_v2/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.


Contributions
-------------

By submitting a contribution to any part of the suite, you license it under
the licence of the part you contribute to AND grant KrakenRF Inc. the rights
described in section 5 ("Contributions") of the KrakenSDR Source Available
Licence (kraken_doa_v2/LICENSE). This lets KrakenRF use the same code in the
GPL programs and in the source-available software.


